# Profile GIF — Instructions

> **Note:** GitHub cannot render animated GIFs directly from SVG files. To create a premium animated `profile.gif`, use one of these methods:

## Option A — Convert an SVG to GIF (Recommended)

Use a free online converter or CLI tool to convert `hologram.svg` (or `ai-core.svg`) into an animated GIF:

1. Open `assets/hologram.svg` in a browser to preview the animation.
2. Use a screen recorder (e.g., OBS, LICEcap) to record the SVG animation.
3. Export the recording as an optimized GIF (240px–480px width, few colors to keep size small).

### CLI (ImageMagick / gifski)
```bash
# Requires the SVG to be rendered first (e.g., via a headless browser)
# Simple approach with conversion tools:
convert assets/hologram.svg -resize 400x400 assets/profile.gif
```

## Option B — Use a canvas-based GIF generator
- Use `Screencastify`, `Kap`, or `GIPHY Capture` to capture the SVG animation.
- Trim and export at small dimensions.

## Option C — Placeholder (works immediately)
If you do not have a GIF yet, the README already references the SVG hologram directly, so the profile still renders beautifully.

---

## Recommended GIF spec
| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Width | 240–480 px |
| Loop | Forever |
| Fps | 12–24 |
| Palette | 32–64 colors |
| File size | < 2 MB (GitHub limit) |

## Customization
Replace `assets/profile.gif` with your generated file. The README references it via:
```md
![Profile](assets/profile.gif)
